   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 06 · Kaggle Training Notebook (Universal Auto-Detection)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook runs entirely in **Kaggle** — no Google Drive connection needed.  \n",
    "It **automatically scans and detects all `.tar` archives** from any dataset folder you uploaded to `/kaggle/input/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Before you start in Kaggle:\n",
    "1. **Add your Data:** Click **\"Add Data\"** (top right sidebar) → attach your uploaded dataset(s) containing your `.tar` files.\n",
    "2. **Enable GPU:** `Settings → Accelerator → GPU P100` (or T4 / 2xT4).\n",
    "3. **Enable Internet:** `Settings → Internet → On` (required for pip packages and GitHub clone).\n",
    "4. Run the cells below in order."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S1 · Clone the GitHub repo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Workspace directories ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "REPO_URL   = 'https://github.com/createsomethingmarvellous/mini-project.git'  # ← your repo\n",
    "BASE       = Path('/kaggle/working/mini_project')\n",
    "FAST       = Path('/kaggle/working/fast')\n",
    "\n",
    "BASE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "FAST.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Optional: GitHub credentials for private repo ──────────────────────────\n",
    "gh_user  = os.environ.get('GITHUB_USER', '')\n",
    "gh_token = os.environ.get('GITHUB_TOKEN', '')\n",
    "\n",
    "if gh_user and gh_token:\n",
    "    with open('/root/.git-credentials', 'w') as f:\n",
    "        f.write(f'https://{gh_user}:{gh_token}@github.com\\n')\n",
    "    os.chmod('/root/.git-credentials', 0o600)\n",
    "    !git config --global credential.helper store\n",
    "    !git config --global user.name \"{gh_user}\"\n",
    "    !git config --global user.email \"{gh_user}@users.noreply.github.com\"\n",
    "    print(f'GitHub credentials configured for: {gh_user} ✓')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Clone or Pull ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "if (BASE / '.git').exists():\n",
    "    print('Repo already exists — fetching latest updates...')\n",
    "    !git -C {BASE} pull -q --rebase\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'Cloning {REPO_URL} into {BASE}...')\n",
    "    !git clone -q {REPO_URL} {BASE}\n",
    "\n",
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "!git log -1 --oneline\n",
    "!ls"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S2 · Install Python packages"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install dependencies for audio augmentation & enhancement\n",
    "!pip install -q audiomentations speechbrain soundfile librosa tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify key libraries\n",
    "!pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i -E \"^(torch|audiomentations|speechbrain|soundfile|librosa|numpy) \"\n",
    "print('\\nPackages ready ✓')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S3 · Inspect GPU, 30 GB RAM, and Attached Kaggle Datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell dynamically searches **all** attached Kaggle input folders to locate your `.tar` archive files."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch, psutil\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── System resource checks ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print('=== System Hardware ===')\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    print(f'GPU Device : {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)} ✓')\n",
    "    print(f'VRAM       : {torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9:.2f} GB')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('⚠️  WARNING: No GPU detected! Enable Accelerator -> GPU in settings.')\n",
    "\n",
    "ram_gb = psutil.virtual_memory().total / 1e9\n",
    "print(f'Total RAM  : {ram_gb:.1f} GB')\n",
    "print(f'CPU Cores  : {os.cpu_count()}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Scan /kaggle/input for datasets and archives ──────────────────────────\n",
    "print('\\n=== Attached Kaggle Datasets & Archives Found ===')\n",
    "input_path = Path('/kaggle/input')\n",
    "if input_path.exists():\n",
    "    all_datasets = [d for d in input_path.iterdir() if d.is_dir()]\n",
    "    for d in all_datasets:\n",
    "        print(f'\\n📁 Dataset folder: {d.name}')\n",
    "        tars = list(d.rglob('*.tar')) + list(d.rglob('*.tar.gz'))\n",
    "        if tars:\n",
    "            for t in tars:\n",
    "                print(f'    📦 Archive: {t.name:<25} ({t.stat().st_size / 1e9:.2f} GB)  at: {t}')\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print('    (no .tar archives found in this dataset folder)')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('⚠️  /kaggle/input not found.')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Show project configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print('\\n=== Project Configuration ===')\n",
    "!python scripts/config.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S4 · Unpack archives to fast NVMe SSD\n",
    "\n",
    "Kaggle datasets are read-only mounted filesystems.  \n",
    "This cell extracts all your audio archives (`asvspoof`, `noise`, `train_aug`, `eval_*`) to the fast NVMe disk (`/kaggle/working/fast`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# scripts/fast_data.py automatically searches all /kaggle/input subfolders!\n",
    "!python scripts/fast_data.py unpack\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nFast local SSD status:')\n",
    "!python scripts/fast_data.py status\n",
    "!du -sh /kaggle/working/fast/* 2>/dev/null || echo ''"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S5 · Setup AASIST & Checkpoints"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import shutil\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Check if AASIST is in any Kaggle input dataset ─────────────────────────\n",
    "aasist_target = BASE / 'aasist'\n",
    "aasist_candidates = list(Path('/kaggle/input').rglob('aasist'))\n",
    "aasist_candidates = [c for c in aasist_candidates if c.is_dir() and (c / 'main.py').exists()]\n",
    "\n",
    "if aasist_target.exists() and (aasist_target / 'main.py').exists():\n",
    "    print('AASIST codebase is already in working directory ✓')\n",
    "elif aasist_candidates:\n",
    "    print(f'Copying AASIST from {aasist_candidates[0]}...')\n",
    "    shutil.copytree(aasist_candidates[0], aasist_target)\n",
    "    print('AASIST copied from Kaggle dataset ✓')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Cloning AASIST repository from GitHub...')\n",
    "    !git clone --depth=1 -q https://github.com/clovaai/aasist.git {aasist_target}\n",
    "    print('Cloned AASIST ✓')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply NumPy compatibility patch\n",
    "print('\\nApplying NumPy patch to AASIST...')\n",
    "!python scripts/setup_aasist.py\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Restore any checkpoints from Kaggle datasets ───────────────────────────\n",
    "ckpt_target = BASE / 'checkpoints'\n",
    "ckpt_candidates = [f for f in Path('/kaggle/input').rglob('*.pt') if 'AASIST.pth' not in f.name]\n",
    "if ckpt_candidates:\n",
    "    print(f'\\nRestoring {len(ckpt_candidates)} checkpoint(s) found in Kaggle inputs...')\n",
    "    for ckpt in ckpt_candidates:\n",
    "        # Put in checkpoints/<seed>/\n",
    "        parent_name = ckpt.parent.name\n",
    "        dst_dir = ckpt_target / parent_name if parent_name.isdigit() else ckpt_target\n",
    "        dst_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "        dst_file = dst_dir / ckpt.name\n",
    "        if not dst_file.exists():\n",
    "            shutil.copy2(ckpt, dst_file)\n",
    "            print(f'  restored: {dst_file.relative_to(BASE)}')\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print(f'  exists:   {dst_file.relative_to(BASE)}')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\\nNo previous checkpoints found in Kaggle inputs (will train from epoch 0).')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Final Pre-flight check ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print('\\n=== Pre-Training Readiness Check ===')\n",
    "checks = {\n",
    "    'AASIST code':          BASE / 'aasist/main.py',\n",
    "    'Model A pretrained':   BASE / 'aasist/models/weights/AASIST.pth',\n",
    "    'ASVspoof training':    FAST / 'asvspoof2019/ASVspoof2019_LA_train',\n",
    "    'ASVspoof dev (eval)':  FAST / 'asvspoof2019/ASVspoof2019_LA_dev',\n",
    "    'MS-SNSD Noise':        FAST / 'MS-SNSD/noise_train',\n",
    "    'Augmented train data': FAST / 'generated/train_aug',\n",
    "    'Eval subset file':     BASE / 'configs/eval_subset_10k.txt',\n",
    "}\n",
    "all_ok = True\n",
    "for label, path in checks.items():\n",
    "    ok = path.exists()\n",
    "    if not ok: all_ok = False\n",
    "    print(f\"  {'OK     ' if ok else 'MISSING'}  {label}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if all_ok:\n",
    "    print('\\n✅ ALL CHECKS PASSED! You are ready to start training with 30GB RAM.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('\\n⚠️  Some files are missing. Check the output of S4 unpack above.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S6 · Run Training (Model B)\n",
    "\n",
    "Kaggle configuration:\n",
    "- `BATCH_SIZE = 32`\n",
    "- `NUM_WORKERS = 4`\n",
    "- `prefetch_factor = 4`\n",
    "- Uses **Focal Loss** ($\gamma=2.0$) & **Frequency Augmentation**\n",
    "- Automatically resumes from last saved checkpoint if interrupted."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Change SEED to 123 or 2024 for subsequent runs\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Starting Model B training with Seed: {SEED}')\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "!python scripts/train_model.py --seed {SEED}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## S7 · Download / Save Trained Checkpoints\n",
    "\n",
    "When your training completes or reaches an epoch you want to keep:  \n",
    "You can find all checkpoints saved at `/kaggle/working/mini_project/checkpoints/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this cell to zip your checkpoints so you can download them directly from the Kaggle **Output** panel on the right sidebar."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import zipfile\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "os.chdir(BASE)\n",
    "\n",
    "ckpt_dir = BASE / 'checkpoints'\n",
    "zip_out = Path('/kaggle/working/trained_checkpoints.zip')\n",
    "\n",
    "if ckpt_dir.exists() and any(ckpt_dir.rglob('*.pt')):\n",
    "    with zipfile.ZipFile(zip_out, 'w', zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as zf:\n",
    "        for f in ckpt_dir.rglob('*'):\n",
    "            if f.is_file():\n",
    "                zf.write(f, arcname=f.relative_to(BASE).as_posix())\n",
    "                print(f'  Zipped: {f.relative_to(BASE)} ({f.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB)')\n",
    "    print(f'\\n✅ Checkpoints bundled to: {zip_out} ({zip_out.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB)')\n",
    "    print('You can download \"trained_checkpoints.zip\" from the Output section in the right sidebar!')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No checkpoints found yet to zip.')"
   ]
  }
 ],
